1
00:00:13,088 --> 00:00:14,916
(This program contains indirect advertisements.)

2
00:00:15,428 --> 00:00:20,498
(The Mullae-dong sky has cleared after the rain.)

3
00:00:20,993 --> 00:00:23,633
- Have you been well?
- I have. Have you?

4
00:00:24,133 --> 00:00:26,033
Yes. Should we speak casually to each other, Hyeong Seo?

5
00:00:26,033 --> 00:00:27,733
- Yes, please do, Kyung Pyo.
- Okay.

6
00:00:27,933 --> 00:00:30,333
- Let's both do.
- Shall we?

7
00:00:31,003 --> 00:00:32,233
- Come on.
- That'd be better, right?

8
00:00:32,433 --> 00:00:33,473
- Come on.
- What?

9
00:00:33,473 --> 00:00:35,103
You're so much older than me.

10
00:00:35,743 --> 00:00:37,273
- Why?
- Are you not?

11
00:00:37,273 --> 00:00:38,543
I was born in 1990.

12
00:00:39,243 --> 00:00:40,313
Am I much older?

13
00:00:40,313 --> 00:00:41,383
- It doesn't matter these days.
- You're eight years older...

14
00:00:41,383 --> 00:00:43,213
- Yes, you're right.
- Yes, it doesn't matter these days.

15
00:00:43,683 --> 00:00:44,813
- People these days all...
- It's just...

16
00:00:44,813 --> 00:00:46,783
I'm worried that I'll forget my manners...

17
00:00:46,783 --> 00:00:48,223
if I start speaking casually to you.

18
00:00:48,383 --> 00:00:49,493
That's fine.

19
00:00:49,693 --> 00:00:51,053
- Shall we, then?
- That's fine.

20
00:00:51,053 --> 00:00:52,863
Okay, Kyung Pyo.

21
00:00:53,393 --> 00:00:55,223
Yes, that's nice.

22
00:00:55,463 --> 00:00:57,493
(They've grown a bit closer.)

23
00:00:57,533 --> 00:00:59,363
- Hello.
- She's here.

24
00:01:00,203 --> 00:01:01,533
- Hello.
- Hi, Kyung Pyo.

25
00:01:01,533 --> 00:01:02,673
- Hello, ma'am.
- Oh, my.

26
00:01:02,833 --> 00:01:03,903
What are you two doing?

27
00:01:03,903 --> 00:01:05,933
- Hey, are we the mafia?
- Hello, ma'am.

28
00:01:05,933 --> 00:01:07,503
(A mafia-like greeting?)

29
00:01:07,743 --> 00:01:08,873
- At rest.
- Yes.

30
00:01:08,873 --> 00:01:10,113
(At rest.)

31
00:01:10,173 --> 00:01:11,643
- Have you been well?
- Yes, I have.

32
00:01:11,643 --> 00:01:13,143
- Have you been well?
- Yes, of course.

33
00:01:13,213 --> 00:01:15,583
Did you tan a bit, Hyeong Seo?

34
00:01:15,583 --> 00:01:17,813
- You're nice and bronzy.
- Right, you're a bit...

35
00:01:18,213 --> 00:01:20,123
Really? Did I tan a bit?

36
00:01:20,123 --> 00:01:21,153
Did you not do anything?

37
00:01:21,153 --> 00:01:22,353
I didn't get a tan.

38
00:01:22,353 --> 00:01:25,393
I just don't wear sunscreen much.

39
00:01:25,493 --> 00:01:27,393
- That's not good.
- But I'm an outdoors person.

40
00:01:27,663 --> 00:01:28,963
- I see.
- An outdoors person.

41
00:01:29,063 --> 00:01:31,063
She must be from a new gang.

42
00:01:31,063 --> 00:01:32,093
The outdoors gang.

43
00:01:32,093 --> 00:01:33,403
(Hello, I'm BIBI from the Outdoors Gang.)

44
00:01:33,403 --> 00:01:35,063
In a moment, someone from the Indoors Gang will be here.

45
00:01:35,063 --> 00:01:36,133
The Indoors Gang.

46
00:01:36,133 --> 00:01:38,503
- Someone who hates summers...
- Yes.

47
00:01:38,703 --> 00:01:39,703
Hello.

48
00:01:39,703 --> 00:01:41,543
- Hello.
- The Indoors Gang is here.

49
00:01:41,703 --> 00:01:43,313
- Hello.
- Come here, Indoors Gang.

50
00:01:43,313 --> 00:01:46,113
- Yes.
- Yes.

51
00:01:46,413 --> 00:01:48,413
Oh, someone is coming today.

52
00:01:48,413 --> 00:01:49,483
Yes, today...

53
00:01:49,483 --> 00:01:50,913
- We have two seats ready.
- Yes, they're coming.

54
00:01:51,053 --> 00:01:52,983
So today, we...

55
00:01:52,983 --> 00:01:55,083
Oh, you really parted your hair right down the middle.

56
00:01:55,083 --> 00:01:56,123
Yes, I did.

57
00:01:56,123 --> 00:01:57,653
I dressed up a bit. Nice and neat.

58
00:01:57,653 --> 00:01:58,853
- Is that so?
- Nice and neat.

59
00:01:58,853 --> 00:02:00,063
- "One and a Half" vibes?
- Yes.

60
00:02:00,063 --> 00:02:01,063
I see.

61
00:02:01,063 --> 00:02:02,693
- The hair from the heyday of idols.
- That's right.

62
00:02:02,693 --> 00:02:04,263
- Like when Sechs Kies debuted.
- It's really annoying.

63
00:02:04,263 --> 00:02:05,263
You're right.

64
00:02:05,263 --> 00:02:06,403
- Like SECHSKIES...
- Moon Hee Joon...

65
00:02:06,403 --> 00:02:08,203
- You're right.
- or Hee Joon.

66
00:02:08,303 --> 00:02:10,603
Or Uhm Jung Hwa when she did "Eyes."

67
00:02:10,803 --> 00:02:13,043
(It's the style from that general era.)

68
00:02:13,403 --> 00:02:15,203
(Suddenly acting seductive)

69
00:02:15,203 --> 00:02:16,443
- I have felt it for a long time - Why are you singing it?

70
00:02:17,113 --> 00:02:18,813
It's just the morning, and I'm already tired.

71
00:02:19,413 --> 00:02:21,583
(This is my joy.)

72
00:02:21,583 --> 00:02:23,083
How have you been, BIBI?

73
00:02:23,083 --> 00:02:24,353
I've been well.

74
00:02:24,353 --> 00:02:26,083
- Really?
- I have,

75
00:02:26,083 --> 00:02:28,583
- but the production team called me.
- What did they say?

76
00:02:28,823 --> 00:02:32,023
They said we would have pretty intense people next time...

77
00:02:32,223 --> 00:02:33,823
and that I should make sure not to be swayed by them.

78
00:02:34,663 --> 00:02:36,463
- They warned me.
- They said that?

79
00:02:36,593 --> 00:02:40,033
We shot with BIBI last time.

80
00:02:40,333 --> 00:02:43,373
- BIBI seems like a strong person, - Yes.

81
00:02:43,373 --> 00:02:44,373
- but she's not really.
- She's not.

82
00:02:44,373 --> 00:02:45,703
- You're right.
- You're right.

83
00:02:45,703 --> 00:02:47,403
She calls herself a Chihuahua.

84
00:02:47,403 --> 00:02:48,403
- In what way?
- She barks easily...

85
00:02:48,403 --> 00:02:49,473
because she gets scared easily.

86
00:02:51,113 --> 00:02:52,943
(Woof!)

87
00:02:52,943 --> 00:02:54,313
(Suddenly barking)

88
00:02:54,313 --> 00:02:55,443
You didn't need to do that.

89
00:02:55,443 --> 00:02:56,683
(We didn't know she was an actual Chihuahua...)

90
00:02:56,683 --> 00:02:58,153
- I saw that side of you.
- Yes.

91
00:02:58,313 --> 00:03:00,953
But today, I'll be bold.

92
00:03:02,353 --> 00:03:03,793
(Screaming)

93
00:03:03,793 --> 00:03:04,793
What did they...

94
00:03:04,793 --> 00:03:06,223
(Screaming out of nowhere)

95
00:03:06,223 --> 00:03:07,963
What did they say to you...

96
00:03:08,293 --> 00:03:10,263
- Oh, so they...
- What did you say?

97
00:03:10,893 --> 00:03:13,563
(It's only the second shoot, and BIBI has become crazy...)

98
00:03:13,803 --> 00:03:15,633
You go first. The pretty one should go first.

99
00:03:17,073 --> 00:03:20,543
Why? You have such a YCC face right now.

100
00:03:20,543 --> 00:03:21,873
- YCC?
- YCC.

101
00:03:22,503 --> 00:03:24,573
- Do I?
- I love places like that.

102
00:03:25,273 --> 00:03:27,183
- Why?
- Because it's hip.

103
00:03:28,083 --> 00:03:29,343
Oh, they're here.

104
00:03:29,343 --> 00:03:31,883
- Are they?
- I got a glance.

105
00:03:32,183 --> 00:03:33,283
(Such strong auras)

106
00:03:33,283 --> 00:03:34,283
Oh, my.

107
00:03:34,853 --> 00:03:36,653
You said, "Oh, my."

108
00:03:37,193 --> 00:03:38,923
- Are you happy I'm here?
- They're here.

109
00:03:39,023 --> 00:03:40,493
- Hello.
- Hello.

110
00:03:40,493 --> 00:03:42,263
- Welcome.
- Are you happy I'm here?

111
00:03:42,933 --> 00:03:44,733
- Hello.
- Oh, my.

112
00:03:45,333 --> 00:03:47,203
- It's been so long, Jeong An.
- Hello.

113
00:03:47,303 --> 00:03:49,003
- Oh, Na Eun's dad!
- Na Eun's dad.

114
00:03:49,003 --> 00:03:50,903
- Nice to meet you.
- Hello.

115
00:03:51,533 --> 00:03:54,443
(The original techno queen that dominated the 2000s)

116
00:03:54,643 --> 00:03:57,913
(An actress who can become any character)

117
00:03:58,173 --> 00:04:00,583
(A naturally funny variety show star)

118
00:04:00,683 --> 00:04:02,513
(The actress who has everything, Chae Jeong An)

119
00:04:02,743 --> 00:04:05,983
(From SHARP, makers of the best hit songs)

120
00:04:06,423 --> 00:04:10,453
(To a solo artist with many great songs)

121
00:04:10,653 --> 00:04:12,823
(Now the mom of two beautiful princesses)

122
00:04:13,323 --> 00:04:14,993
(Everyone's witty and charming older sister)

123
00:04:14,993 --> 00:04:17,133
(Lee Ji Hye)

124
00:04:17,133 --> 00:04:19,763
- I love this.
- They dominated the 2000s.

125
00:04:19,763 --> 00:04:22,163
- She's still popular today.
- She's a member of SHARP.

126
00:04:22,163 --> 00:04:25,303
By the way, aren't you two very close?

127
00:04:25,303 --> 00:04:26,873
- We met each other before marriage.
- Before marriage.

128
00:04:26,873 --> 00:04:27,873
- I see.
- Yes.

129
00:04:27,873 --> 00:04:28,973
They're clubbing buddies.

130
00:04:29,773 --> 00:04:31,813
- It's karaoke.
- They're karaoke buddies.

131
00:04:31,873 --> 00:04:33,343
(Karaoke buddies instead of clubbing buddies?)

132
00:04:33,343 --> 00:04:34,913
- Karaoke buddies.
- Karaoke buddies.

133
00:04:34,913 --> 00:04:36,913
- Karaoke buddies?
- Karaoke buddies.

134
00:04:37,113 --> 00:04:39,313
You know where the word "karaoke" comes from?

135
00:04:39,783 --> 00:04:41,423
- Fake orchestra.
- Fake orchestra.

136
00:04:41,953 --> 00:04:44,293
- Oh, my. I see.
- Actually...

137
00:04:44,323 --> 00:04:45,593
Back then, there were so many...

138
00:04:45,593 --> 00:04:47,223
- karaoke bars in Cheongdam-dong.
- There were so many.

139
00:04:47,223 --> 00:04:49,493
That was a time...

140
00:04:49,833 --> 00:04:51,193
when a lot of people went...

141
00:04:51,193 --> 00:04:52,863
- to karaoke often.
- That's right.

142
00:04:52,963 --> 00:04:54,833
That's not where we met.

143
00:04:54,833 --> 00:04:56,873
We actually met in the restroom at a broadcasting station.

144
00:04:56,933 --> 00:04:59,473
- Did you almost get into a fight?
- Is that right?

145
00:04:59,473 --> 00:05:00,803
No, I mean...

146
00:05:00,943 --> 00:05:02,103
Did one of you say...

147
00:05:02,103 --> 00:05:03,773
- "come outside?"
- I don't always get into fights.

148
00:05:03,943 --> 00:05:05,673
- So that's not what happened?
- No.

149
00:05:05,673 --> 00:05:07,213
I went to the restroom,

150
00:05:07,343 --> 00:05:09,213
and I saw a beautiful woman there.

151
00:05:09,213 --> 00:05:10,983
You know how you can feel...

152
00:05:10,983 --> 00:05:12,183
someone's energy when you see them?

153
00:05:12,183 --> 00:05:15,153
I thought that I could become friends with her.

154
00:05:15,323 --> 00:05:16,953
That day, she asked me to go to karaoke with her.

155
00:05:18,223 --> 00:05:19,523
- Right.
- What year was that?

156
00:05:20,463 --> 00:05:21,993
It was 2000.

157
00:05:21,993 --> 00:05:24,093
- That was 26 years ago.
- Or was it 1999?

158
00:05:24,093 --> 00:05:25,463
No, it was 2000.

159
00:05:25,533 --> 00:05:28,033
I was a 1st album singer, and she was a 2nd album singer.

160
00:05:28,033 --> 00:05:29,163
She was number one on the charts.

161
00:05:29,163 --> 00:05:30,273
(1st album singer, Jeong An, Number 1 singer, Ji Hye)

162
00:05:30,273 --> 00:05:31,503
- Actually...
- You were very popular.

163
00:05:31,503 --> 00:05:32,773
I was slightly more established...

164
00:05:32,973 --> 00:05:33,973
at that time.

165
00:05:33,973 --> 00:05:35,673
I wanted to become closer to the number one singer,

166
00:05:35,673 --> 00:05:38,173
so I was kind to her in the restroom.

167
00:05:39,413 --> 00:05:40,583
The drinks are here.

168
00:05:40,683 --> 00:05:42,513
- Is this with lots of caffeine?
- Yes.

169
00:05:42,513 --> 00:05:43,953
- That's for Kyung Pyo.
- It has a lot of caffeine.

170
00:05:44,213 --> 00:05:46,623
Usually around this time of day,

171
00:05:46,623 --> 00:05:48,623
wouldn't you still be in bed?

172
00:05:48,623 --> 00:05:51,153
I'm usually up, but I came back from Japan late last night.

173
00:05:51,153 --> 00:05:53,423
I see. You need to get over the jet lag.

174
00:05:53,563 --> 00:05:54,593
Jet lag?

175
00:05:54,593 --> 00:05:55,663
- Jeong An.
- Yes?

176
00:05:55,663 --> 00:05:56,993
You were probably joking,

177
00:05:56,993 --> 00:05:58,863
but there's no time difference between here and Japan.

178
00:05:58,863 --> 00:06:00,603
I know, but that's not the case with China.

179
00:06:00,863 --> 00:06:02,233
- There's a time difference there.
- One hour.

180
00:06:02,233 --> 00:06:03,803
- Right.
- I found out recently.

181
00:06:04,403 --> 00:06:05,873
We can't exactly call one hour...

182
00:06:05,873 --> 00:06:07,643
- That's true.
- a time difference.

183
00:06:07,743 --> 00:06:09,403
But meal times are important.

184
00:06:09,843 --> 00:06:11,173
What kind of conversation is this?

185
00:06:11,943 --> 00:06:14,083
Anyone listening would think that I really don't know.

186
00:06:15,343 --> 00:06:16,813
I know there's no time difference.

187
00:06:17,613 --> 00:06:19,383
I was there last month.

188
00:06:19,383 --> 00:06:21,953
- Where?
- Tokyo. Ginza.

189
00:06:22,853 --> 00:06:23,893
What did you do there?

190
00:06:24,393 --> 00:06:25,423
I went shopping.

191
00:06:25,993 --> 00:06:28,463
(Her way of speaking is strangely charming.)

192
00:06:28,463 --> 00:06:29,663
That's great.

193
00:06:29,693 --> 00:06:30,763
What is today's theme?

194
00:06:31,063 --> 00:06:33,433
The theme of today's second episode is...

195
00:06:33,433 --> 00:06:35,463
The Owner Who's Serious About "Mi."

196
00:06:35,463 --> 00:06:37,033
- What?
- "Mi?"

197
00:06:37,033 --> 00:06:38,433
- "Mi" that means taste?
- What?

198
00:06:38,573 --> 00:06:40,473
- It could also mean beautiful.
- Is it beautiful or taste?

199
00:06:40,473 --> 00:06:42,343
- We don't know which one it is.
- "Mi" could also mean rice.

200
00:06:42,343 --> 00:06:43,343
That's right.

201
00:06:43,443 --> 00:06:44,813
- My gosh.
- Rice.

202
00:06:45,673 --> 00:06:47,043
That's amazing.

203
00:06:47,043 --> 00:06:48,813
Is that a hint for today?

204
00:06:49,313 --> 00:06:51,053
We tried this...

205
00:06:51,053 --> 00:06:53,183
for the first time last week.

206
00:06:53,623 --> 00:06:54,783
We were very surprised last week.

207
00:06:54,953 --> 00:06:56,793
Yes, it was very surprising.

208
00:06:56,793 --> 00:06:57,793
They're cassette tapes.

209
00:06:57,793 --> 00:07:00,093
B-Side is the theme of the show this season.

210
00:07:00,093 --> 00:07:01,163
(Important clues of on-site audio from each of the three places)

211
00:07:01,163 --> 00:07:02,563
We have to listen to these carefully.

212
00:07:02,623 --> 00:07:03,663
These will be hints.

213
00:07:03,763 --> 00:07:06,663
We got it right last time during the first episode.

214
00:07:06,803 --> 00:07:08,403
- Yes.
- We almost got it wrong,

215
00:07:08,403 --> 00:07:09,803
but BIBI was very sharp.

216
00:07:10,133 --> 00:07:11,433
- So you're sharp.
- She convinced us otherwise.

217
00:07:11,433 --> 00:07:13,603
You gave it to me because it was my first time.

218
00:07:13,903 --> 00:07:15,773
- No.
- No, we had no idea.

219
00:07:16,273 --> 00:07:18,013
She definitely looks like the smartest one here.

220
00:07:18,343 --> 00:07:19,413
- Really?
- I agree.

221
00:07:19,513 --> 00:07:20,513
What do you think about me?

222
00:07:21,143 --> 00:07:22,443
I need some time to get to know you.

223
00:07:23,683 --> 00:07:26,353
(The longer you look, the prettier he gets.)

224
00:07:27,083 --> 00:07:28,423
- Let's listen to it.
- Okay.

225
00:07:28,983 --> 00:07:29,993
It's the first one.

226
00:07:30,393 --> 00:07:31,923
(First store, a clue from the on-site reaction)

227
00:07:31,923 --> 00:07:33,823
- Encore - Encore

228
00:07:34,193 --> 00:07:37,493
- One more song - One more song

229
00:07:37,493 --> 00:07:38,533
"One more song?"

230
00:07:39,193 --> 00:07:40,863
"Encore, encore, one more song."

231
00:07:40,863 --> 00:07:41,963
- What?
- Right?

232
00:07:41,963 --> 00:07:44,133
(What does it have to do with "mi?")

233
00:07:44,303 --> 00:07:45,373
It's related to music.

234
00:07:45,373 --> 00:07:46,573
After saying encore,

235
00:07:46,573 --> 00:07:48,373
- they said, "One more song."
- Right.

236
00:07:48,373 --> 00:07:49,703
- Yes.
- Is it related to concerts?

237
00:07:49,873 --> 00:07:52,013
All right, this is the second one.

238
00:07:52,013 --> 00:07:53,383
(Let's listen to the clue from the second location.)

239
00:07:53,413 --> 00:07:56,383
(Second store, a clue from the on-site reaction)

240
00:07:56,383 --> 00:07:58,913
Cooking is complete.

241
00:07:58,913 --> 00:08:00,283
Is parking complete?

242
00:08:00,283 --> 00:08:01,983
- Cooking.
- Cooking is complete.

243
00:08:02,123 --> 00:08:03,353
It's the sound of a rice cooker.

244
00:08:03,353 --> 00:08:05,023
- This is...
- It's like the one at my house.

245
00:08:05,023 --> 00:08:06,463
- a classic rice cooker sound.
- Right.

246
00:08:06,463 --> 00:08:08,423
- It said, "Cook, cook, cooking."
- Yes.

247
00:08:08,493 --> 00:08:10,393
Rice "mi" could be the answer.

248
00:08:10,393 --> 00:08:11,463
Right.

249
00:08:11,633 --> 00:08:13,103
This is the third and the last one.

250
00:08:13,803 --> 00:08:16,533
(Third store, a clue from the on-site reaction)

251
00:08:16,533 --> 00:08:18,673
(Groaning)

252
00:08:18,933 --> 00:08:20,043
Bubbles...

