00:17:48,343 --> 00:17:49,673
- It's good.
- Great.

513
00:17:50,513 --> 00:17:53,643
If you write down a song request,

514
00:17:53,643 --> 00:17:56,213
- The beef tripe song.
- I'll sing while you eat.

515
00:17:56,213 --> 00:17:57,283
Okay.

516
00:17:57,283 --> 00:17:58,483
If you write down 3 to 4 songs,

517
00:17:58,483 --> 00:17:59,783
I'll sing one I know.

518
00:18:01,283 --> 00:18:02,753
Here's what I want to listen to.

519
00:18:02,753 --> 00:18:04,693
- It was written on his apron.
- I see.

520
00:18:04,693 --> 00:18:06,493
"My Whole World."

521
00:18:06,723 --> 00:18:07,823
- "My Whole World."
- I love that song.

522
00:18:07,823 --> 00:18:09,163
You're getting teary just from the song title.

523
00:18:09,163 --> 00:18:10,263
I don't know what's up with me.

524
00:18:10,263 --> 00:18:12,133
The title itself is already heart-wrenching.

525
00:18:12,363 --> 00:18:14,063
- You're a feeler, right?
- You must be a feeler.

526
00:18:14,063 --> 00:18:15,063
Bringing it up was...

527
00:18:15,063 --> 00:18:16,603
What's wrong? This isn't the last episode.

528
00:18:16,603 --> 00:18:18,003
It must be because I'm hungry.

529
00:18:18,003 --> 00:18:20,403
- Is it because you're hungry?
- Let's get her some food.

530
00:18:20,403 --> 00:18:21,873
And "Heartless" by Chae Jeong An.

531
00:18:21,873 --> 00:18:23,713
- Jeong An's songs are nice.
- They have fun beats.

532
00:18:23,713 --> 00:18:25,313
(Added "Heartless" by Chae Jeong An,)

533
00:18:25,313 --> 00:18:27,113
(completing the beef tripe song request)

534
00:18:27,113 --> 00:18:28,343
He's cooking now.

535
00:18:28,513 --> 00:18:30,683
- You can see him in real time.
- Right.

536
00:18:31,653 --> 00:18:33,413
- My gosh.
- Being able to see...

537
00:18:33,413 --> 00:18:36,283
- everything while eating...
- It's like live streaming.

538
00:18:36,283 --> 00:18:38,353
- helps build trust.
- True.

539
00:18:39,653 --> 00:18:42,663
(Let's get to grilling the beef tripe.)

540
00:18:43,193 --> 00:18:45,893
Wouldn't beef tripe become more popular?

541
00:18:45,893 --> 00:18:46,893
(Hoping beef tripe would go global)

542
00:18:46,893 --> 00:18:49,463
That's how I came up with the beef tripe platter.

543
00:18:49,463 --> 00:18:50,573
(The owner's ambitious menu)

544
00:18:50,803 --> 00:18:53,633
(To the pre-grilled beef tripe,)

545
00:18:54,603 --> 00:18:58,473
(he adds a secret sauce to boost the smoky flavor!)

546
00:18:58,643 --> 00:19:01,783
As for pane gopchang, I add the gopchang to bread.

547
00:19:01,783 --> 00:19:04,183
You mix in the cheese and have it with bread.

548
00:19:05,853 --> 00:19:08,653
As for the green onion makchang, it's like Japanese negi makchang.

549
00:19:10,353 --> 00:19:13,653
You make a wrap out of the green onion,

550
00:19:13,653 --> 00:19:15,093
makchang, and teriyaki sauce.

551
00:19:15,323 --> 00:19:17,633
Those two foods make up the platter.

552
00:19:17,633 --> 00:19:19,533
(This is the beef tripe platter.)

553
00:19:19,533 --> 00:19:22,263
It's a menu that expands Korean cuisine into...

554
00:19:22,263 --> 00:19:23,563
Western and Japanese cuisine.

555
00:19:24,103 --> 00:19:25,503
Here's your order.

556
00:19:25,503 --> 00:19:26,573
Oh, my.

557
00:19:27,003 --> 00:19:28,803
- Is this the platter?
- Yes, it is.

558
00:19:28,943 --> 00:19:30,773
- My gosh.
- It looks good.

559
00:19:30,973 --> 00:19:32,643
The pane is a pig's face.

560
00:19:32,873 --> 00:19:34,313
It's a pig's face viewed from above.

561
00:19:34,483 --> 00:19:35,583
The pane?

562
00:19:35,583 --> 00:19:37,383
- These are the ears.
- The ears and face.

563
00:19:37,383 --> 00:19:38,583
- Correct.
- How cute.

564
00:19:38,583 --> 00:19:39,883
Incredible. Thank you.

565
00:19:39,883 --> 00:19:41,283
(The plating showcases the owner's creativity.)

566
00:19:41,283 --> 00:19:44,353
I was going to eat in moderation today.

567
00:19:44,353 --> 00:19:45,453
But I won't be able to.

568
00:19:45,653 --> 00:19:46,753
There's no moderation here.

569
00:19:47,463 --> 00:19:48,823
Place it on top.

570
00:19:48,823 --> 00:19:50,693
Place a piece of gopchang on top.

571
00:19:50,833 --> 00:19:52,293
Like so.

572
00:19:52,593 --> 00:19:53,733
- Separately.
- Separately?

573
00:19:53,733 --> 00:19:54,963
- Yes.
- I see.

574
00:19:54,963 --> 00:19:56,733
(Taking a bite)

575
00:19:56,733 --> 00:19:58,273
Look at the cheese.

576
00:19:58,673 --> 00:20:00,103
It's giving off rice cake vibes.

577
00:20:00,233 --> 00:20:01,243
Is this gopchang?

578
00:20:01,243 --> 00:20:02,703
(Smiling)

579
00:20:02,843 --> 00:20:04,073
Is this gopchang?

580
00:20:08,843 --> 00:20:10,413
- How is it?
- It doesn't smell meaty at all.

581
00:20:10,413 --> 00:20:12,153
(Packed with smoky flavors without a meaty smell)

582
00:20:13,083 --> 00:20:16,623
(Impossible to let go of)

583
00:20:16,623 --> 00:20:17,993
- It's good.
- It's good.

584
00:20:18,323 --> 00:20:19,553
It's really good.

585
00:20:19,553 --> 00:20:21,793
- Right?
- This menu alone must attract...

586
00:20:21,793 --> 00:20:22,793
a lot of customers.

587
00:20:22,793 --> 00:20:24,393
(A flavor that drives views)

588
00:20:24,633 --> 00:20:26,133
It's a classic example of today's food trends.

589
00:20:26,163 --> 00:20:27,603
The gopchang sauce is delicious.

590
00:20:27,863 --> 00:20:30,203
In other words, the food isn't tailored to us.

591
00:20:31,403 --> 00:20:32,903
(Crying)

592
00:20:33,203 --> 00:20:35,003
We've got some oldies here, don't we?

593
00:20:36,203 --> 00:20:37,913
- Who?
- I won't say who.

594
00:20:37,913 --> 00:20:40,213
- Who?
- The ratio would be four to...

595
00:20:41,213 --> 00:20:42,243
How cold of you.

596
00:20:43,383 --> 00:20:44,383
Four to...

597
00:20:44,383 --> 00:20:46,253
(I'm not one of the oldies.)

598
00:20:46,483 --> 00:20:48,723
Everyone, are you enjoying the food?

599
00:20:48,723 --> 00:20:49,853
- Yes!
- Yes!

600
00:20:49,853 --> 00:20:51,753
It's time for the beef tripe song.

601
00:20:51,753 --> 00:20:54,063
I'm going to sing a song you've requested.

602
00:20:54,063 --> 00:20:55,123
- Which one will he sing?
- May I?

603
00:20:55,123 --> 00:20:56,123
- Yes.
- Go ahead.

604
00:20:56,123 --> 00:20:57,233
Thank you.

605
00:20:57,233 --> 00:21:00,393
How could I pass up the chance to sing a song by the beautiful...

606
00:21:00,393 --> 00:21:01,603
Chae Jeong An, who's here today?

607
00:21:01,603 --> 00:21:03,803
Here's "Heartless" by Chae Jeong An.

608
00:21:04,233 --> 00:21:05,373
Please enjoy.

609
00:21:05,373 --> 00:21:06,533
(It's my song.)

610
00:21:06,533 --> 00:21:07,643
"Heartless."

611
00:21:07,643 --> 00:21:09,273
I didn't think I'd get to hear it here.

612
00:21:09,273 --> 00:21:11,113
("Heartless" by Chae Jeong An)

613
00:21:11,473 --> 00:21:12,913
This song gets you pumped up.

614
00:21:13,813 --> 00:21:14,813
(Cheering)

615
00:21:15,213 --> 00:21:16,283
I love it.

616
00:21:16,583 --> 00:21:19,683
(Speaking of "Heartless...")

617
00:21:20,253 --> 00:21:23,223
(Shaking up late-1990s Korea,)

618
00:21:23,953 --> 00:21:26,223
(a techno warrior appeared.)

619
00:21:27,723 --> 00:21:29,563
(Let's go back 30 years!)

620
00:21:29,863 --> 00:21:31,563
(Take me with you!)

621
00:21:31,563 --> 00:21:33,533
(In a trance)

622
00:21:33,533 --> 00:21:35,163
(Singing)

623
00:21:35,503 --> 00:21:36,833
Listen to that ad-lib!

624
00:21:37,573 --> 00:21:40,873
(I did everything you wanted me to)

625
00:21:40,873 --> 00:21:44,273
(I didn't do anything you hated)

626
00:21:44,443 --> 00:21:45,513
Your!

627
00:21:45,513 --> 00:21:46,973
Isn't that the original key?

628
00:21:47,883 --> 00:21:49,743
(The original techno queen is here.)

629
00:21:49,743 --> 00:21:51,513
(Whether I love you or not!)

630
00:21:51,513 --> 00:21:53,153
(Getting excited)

631
00:21:53,153 --> 00:21:54,983
(This is so much fun.)

632
00:21:54,983 --> 00:21:58,553
(I could tell even if you played innocent)

633
00:21:58,953 --> 00:22:00,963
(Bold and sexy)

634
00:22:02,323 --> 00:22:03,563
(Husky)

635
00:22:03,563 --> 00:22:04,693
(The love is beyond comprehension.)

636
00:22:04,693 --> 00:22:06,093
You two have good chemistry.

637
00:22:06,093 --> 00:22:07,133
(Dancing the day away)

638
00:22:07,263 --> 00:22:09,763
(The perfect partner)

639
00:22:10,733 --> 00:22:12,473
(Cheering)

640
00:22:13,803 --> 00:22:15,443
(Tripe Chang Suk is beyond amazing.)

641
00:22:15,443 --> 00:22:17,203
He's good.

642
00:22:18,043 --> 00:22:19,843
Thank you. That was the beef tripe song.

643
00:22:21,113 --> 00:22:23,443
(The owner leaves.)

644
00:22:23,443 --> 00:22:24,753
It's nice to hear it again after so long.

645
00:22:24,753 --> 00:22:26,953
- It's a masterpiece, right?
- Yes, it is.

646
00:22:26,953 --> 00:22:28,353
(He acknowledges "Heartless.")

647
00:22:28,353 --> 00:22:29,753
Really, it's a masterpiece.

648
00:22:29,753 --> 00:22:31,353
- Of course.
- It's a fun song.

649
00:22:31,353 --> 00:22:33,793
I saw Ji Hye from the 2000s again after so long.

650
00:22:35,423 --> 00:22:37,063
For a good while, her life was all about...

651
00:22:37,063 --> 00:22:39,533
"Tae Ri."

652
00:22:39,933 --> 00:22:41,033
True.

653
00:22:41,033 --> 00:22:42,633
- It brought back memories.
- Right?

654
00:22:42,633 --> 00:22:44,503
- It did.
- You went to Ppeokkugi, right?

655
00:22:44,503 --> 00:22:46,003
Ppeokkugi and Switch It Up.

656
00:22:48,043 --> 00:22:50,303
Hearing that helped me remember the name.

657
00:22:50,443 --> 00:22:52,173
What kind of beer snacks did you like?

658
00:22:52,173 --> 00:22:55,913
I used to go for meat.

659
00:22:55,913 --> 00:22:57,513
I liked Lord Park's.

660
00:22:57,513 --> 00:22:59,113
You went to places...

661
00:22:59,113 --> 00:23:00,983
that were quite pricey.

662
00:23:00,983 --> 00:23:03,053
I liked people who were a little well off.

663
00:23:05,953 --> 00:23:09,693
(Deeply touching)

664
00:23:09,693 --> 00:23:11,093
I was broke.

665
00:23:11,093 --> 00:23:12,663
I wanted the others to be well off.

666
00:23:12,663 --> 00:23:15,003
- I can totally relate to that.
- Right?

667
00:23:15,003 --> 00:23:16,633
Jae Seok was penniless,

668
00:23:16,633 --> 00:23:18,833
so he asked the others for a ride to nightclubs.

669
00:23:19,033 --> 00:23:20,903
- Those were the days.
- Those were the days.

670
00:23:21,203 --> 00:23:22,643
- Yes.
- That's unexpected.

671
00:23:22,643 --> 00:23:23,803
- How so?
- I didn't think you went clubbing.

672
00:23:23,803 --> 00:23:25,573
I loved going to nightclubs.

673
00:23:26,343 --> 00:23:27,643
- Don't you know...
- That's new.

674
00:23:27,643 --> 00:23:28,943
Nallari Yu Jae Seok?

675
00:23:29,483 --> 00:23:30,813
- Nallari Yu Jae Seok.
- Nallari.

676
00:23:30,813 --> 00:23:32,383
It was such a fun time.

677
00:23:32,613 --> 00:23:35,353
You know that thing at nightclubs.

678
00:23:35,353 --> 00:23:38,253
- Matchmaking?
- Yes, matchmaking. That system.

679
00:23:38,253 --> 00:23:39,793
System. Yes, the system.

680
00:23:39,793 --> 00:23:41,223
- System.
- The matchmaking system.

681
00:23:41,223 --> 00:23:43,423
Personally, I want it to return.

682
00:23:43,423 --> 00:23:44,463
It's nice.

683
00:23:44,763 --> 00:23:46,563
Listen, BIBI. That system existed,

684
00:23:46,563 --> 00:23:48,433
but some people never experienced it.

685
00:23:48,433 --> 00:23:51,303
(Not everyone could enjoy the matchmaking system.)

686
00:23:51,473 --> 00:23:52,473
(Solemn)

687
00:23:52,473 --> 00:23:54,043
"Where are they going?"

688
00:23:54,043 --> 00:23:55,743
"Why are they leaving and heading over there?"

689
00:23:55,743 --> 00:23:57,813
I always saw them leave and stayed where I always was.

690
00:23:57,813 --> 00:23:59,273
(But I remained exactly where I was.)

691
00:23:59,273 --> 00:24:01,183
That's why Eun I's table never got robbed.

692
00:24:01,683 --> 00:24:03,143
I watched everyone's bags.

693
00:24:03,583 --> 00:24:04,583
I watched them all.

694
00:24:04,583 --> 00:24:06,383
- The safe zone.
- I watched all the bags.

695
00:24:06,383 --> 00:24:07,683
- Of course.
- There were no thefts.

696
00:24:08,153 --> 00:24:09,783
This feels like a drinking party.

697
00:24:09,783 --> 00:24:10,793
- You're right.
- It's fun.

698
00:24:10,793 --> 00:24:12,693
This all started with "Heartless."

699
00:24:12,693 --> 00:24:13,993
Totally.

700
00:24:13,993 --> 00:24:16,293
- You're right.
- The owner singing "Heartless..."

701
00:24:16,293 --> 00:24:17,563
- was a trip down memory lane.
- Yes.

702
00:24:17,563 --> 00:24:19,663
- I get the power of songs now.
- For real.

703
00:24:19,833 --> 00:24:20,863
(Applauding)

704
00:24:20,863 --> 00:24:21,863
- This place is...
- Really.

705
00:24:21,963 --> 00:24:23,763
This is Sixth Sense.

706
00:24:23,763 --> 00:24:26,373
We're enjoying ourselves a little too much...

707
00:24:26,373 --> 00:24:27,843
as if this place were actually real.

708
00:24:27,843 --> 00:24:28,843
- For real.
- Right.

709
00:24:28,843 --> 00:24:30,073
Shouldn't we...

710
00:24:30,073 --> 00:24:31,743
- There's not an ounce of doubt.
- No.

711
00:24:31,743 --> 00:24:33,373
Actually, if you think about it carefully,

712
00:24:34,043 --> 00:24:36,113
if the production crew wanted to install that,

713
00:24:36,113 --> 00:24:37,183
they totally could have.

714
00:24:37,183 --> 00:24:38,653
True.

715
00:24:39,383 --> 00:24:41,683
- All they needed was a kitchen.
- All they needed was a kitchen...

716
00:24:41,683 --> 00:24:42,783
to install the monitor and all.

717
00:24:43,553 --> 00:24:44,653
(This place is fake!)

718
00:24:44,653 --> 00:24:46,993
(The production crew installed the sound equipment?)

719
00:24:46,993 --> 00:24:48,923
I find it weird that the floor isn't greasy.

720
00:24:48,923 --> 00:24:49,963
- Exactly.
- Right?

721
00:24:50,193 --> 00:24:52,233
- The floor isn't greasy at all.
- Beef tripe places are...

722
00:24:52,233 --> 00:24:53,563
- usually greasy.
- It's greasy.

723
00:24:53,563 --> 00:24:57,233
(The tripe place has a surprisingly spotless, grease-free floor.)

724
00:24:58,203 --> 00:24:59,873
- It's...
- This one is quite tough.

725
00:25:00,503 --> 00:25:02,003
- Got it. Next.
- Okay.

726
00:25:02,003 --> 00:25:03,643
- Let's find Mi.
- Mi.

727
00:25:03,643 --> 00:25:05,013
(The Singing Do-Re-Mi Owner)

728
00:25:05,013 --> 00:25:06,343
(A tripe place with no grease on the floor)

729
00:25:06,343 --> 00:25:07,583
- It's not easy.
- No, it isn't.

730
00:25:07,583 --> 00:25:10,343
- It's not easy.
- Last week,

731
00:25:10,813 --> 00:25:12,453
we got it right out of pure luck.

732
00:25:12,783 --> 00:25:14,253
Last week's scale was on a different level.

733
00:25:14,253 --> 00:25:15,283
- Totally.
- Yes.

734
00:25:15,283 --> 00:25:16,723
- There were too many cast members.
- Around...

735
00:25:16,723 --> 00:25:18,223
What's more, all 100 citizens we met...

736
00:25:18,223 --> 00:25:20,993
were cast members chosen by our production crew.

737
00:25:20,993 --> 00:25:21,993
(Surprised)

738
00:25:22,093 --> 00:25:23,463
- Really?
- It was no joke.

739
00:25:23,463 --> 00:25:25,163
This show is like a blockbuster.

740
00:25:25,163 --> 00:25:26,633
- It's "The Trulyman Show."
- Right?

741
00:25:26,633 --> 00:25:27,703
I agree.

742
00:25:28,633 --> 00:25:30,263
It's "The Truman Show," not "The Trulyman Show."

743
00:25:30,263 --> 00:25:31,273
Gosh.

744
00:25:31,433 --> 00:25:33,003
(Oh, no!)

745
00:25:33,003 --> 00:25:34,873
I thought she said it on purpose.

746
00:25:34,873 --> 00:25:36,373
Did you just cuss?

747
00:25:36,503 --> 00:25:38,873
I classify the traits of people who make others laugh...

748
00:25:38,873 --> 00:25:40,773
into three categories.

749
00:25:40,813 --> 00:25:42,543
Jeong An is one of them.

750
00:25:42,683 --> 00:25:44,253
No matter what she does,

751
00:25:44,253 --> 00:25:45,713
people find it funny.

752
00:25:45,713 --> 00:25:46,713
(Is that so?)

753
00:25:46,913 --> 00:25:48,523
(Living proof)

754
00:25:48,523 --> 00:25:51,123
- I have this weird obsession.
- What is it?

755
00:25:51,493 --> 00:25:53,923
Because I have this great urge to be funny,

756
00:25:53,923 --> 00:25:55,023
I don't laugh when others are...

757
00:25:55,023 --> 00:25:56,163
- being funny.
- You don't laugh.

758
00:25:56,163 --> 00:25:57,933
- No.
- Are you the envious type?

759
00:25:58,133 --> 00:26:00,333
Rather than that, I compete against them all by myself.

760
00:26:00,663 --> 00:26:01,763
I get it.

761
00:26:02,103 --> 00:26:03,103
It's just...

762
00:26:03,103 --> 00:26:04,633
- But...
- Do you think to yourself,

763
00:26:04,633 --> 00:26:05,773
"Why didn't I say that?"

764
00:26:05,773 --> 00:26:07,573
Let go of the need to compete so much.

765
00:26:07,743 --> 00:26:08,803
- Relax.
- I competed against you...

766
00:26:08,803 --> 00:26:09,843
in the past,

767
00:26:09,843 --> 00:26:11,773
but you were better than me.

768
00:26:11,773 --> 00:26:12,913
Are you acknowledging it?

769
00:26:13,213 --> 00:26:15,743
Are you accepting defeat?

770
00:26:15,743 --> 00:26:17,213
- But you're prettier.
