Smelling myself neutralizes my senses.

1027
00:34:49,863 --> 00:34:51,393
What happens if you smell my skin?

1028
00:34:51,393 --> 00:34:52,463
(Disgusted)

1029
00:34:52,593 --> 00:34:54,263
- So...
- What happens if you smell my skin?

1030
00:34:55,463 --> 00:34:58,003
(Forget me "Letter" by Chae Jeong An)

1031
00:34:58,433 --> 00:34:59,803
Great joke, Jeong An.

1032
00:35:00,303 --> 00:35:02,473
Keep up the good work!

1033
00:35:02,743 --> 00:35:04,243
- Great joke.
- It really was.

1034
00:35:04,243 --> 00:35:05,513
(She focuses again despite the sabotage.)

1035
00:35:05,643 --> 00:35:06,773
I know this one.

1036
00:35:07,573 --> 00:35:09,043
I think it's short-grain rice.

1037
00:35:09,243 --> 00:35:12,113
(Did she really get it right this time too?)

1038
00:35:12,383 --> 00:35:13,813
I think it's short-grain rice.

1039
00:35:13,953 --> 00:35:15,023
- Correct!
- You got it.

1040
00:35:15,723 --> 00:35:17,323
(Easily gets 2 in a row)

1041
00:35:17,323 --> 00:35:18,623
I can't believe it.

1042
00:35:18,853 --> 00:35:20,023
It smells like popcorn.

1043
00:35:20,153 --> 00:35:21,223
I can't believe it.

1044
00:35:21,253 --> 00:35:23,423
Popcorn? Is it buttery?

1045
00:35:24,163 --> 00:35:25,193
She's right!

1046
00:35:25,193 --> 00:35:27,163
(She sniffs it like she was taught.)

1047
00:35:27,163 --> 00:35:28,203
It really smells different.

1048
00:35:28,663 --> 00:35:30,563
(Sniffing)

1049
00:35:30,733 --> 00:35:32,133
(Tilting)

1050
00:35:32,533 --> 00:35:35,073
(She takes one careful bite,)

1051
00:35:35,443 --> 00:35:40,343
(then keeps smelling without answering.)

1052
00:35:42,443 --> 00:35:45,783
This is either Dalhami or Yeonjin rice.

1053
00:35:45,783 --> 00:35:47,113
But I'm not sure.

1054
00:35:48,553 --> 00:35:50,053
(He peeks at the answer.)

1055
00:35:50,053 --> 00:35:52,323
(Amazed)

1056
00:35:52,353 --> 00:35:55,293
(The answer was Yeonjin rice, just like she said!)

1057
00:35:55,493 --> 00:35:58,833
(The fact that she's even torn is surprising to them.)

1058
00:35:58,833 --> 00:36:00,333
I don't think I'll get this one right.

1059
00:36:00,563 --> 00:36:02,003
- I want to say Dalhami rice.
- Dalhami?

1060
00:36:02,163 --> 00:36:04,033
- Am I wrong?
- Let's see.

1061
00:36:04,163 --> 00:36:05,173
- It was Yeonjin rice.
- Yeonjin!

1062
00:36:05,173 --> 00:36:06,803
But you said it was either Dalhami or Yeonjin!

1063
00:36:06,803 --> 00:36:09,443
- I got chills when you said it!
- Me too!

1064
00:36:09,773 --> 00:36:11,473
We'll put it down as Yeonjin.

1065
00:36:11,473 --> 00:36:12,543
That's good!

1066
00:36:13,243 --> 00:36:14,243
Don't worry.

1067
00:36:14,243 --> 00:36:15,913
Is this Yudel rice?

1068
00:36:16,343 --> 00:36:17,413
- Correct.
- Gosh!

1069
00:36:18,353 --> 00:36:19,353
Dalhami rice?

1070
00:36:19,753 --> 00:36:20,813
- Dalhami!
- Correct!

1071
00:36:21,523 --> 00:36:23,083
(Her final score is 4 out of 5!)

1072
00:36:23,083 --> 00:36:24,353
Look, I got chills!

1073
00:36:24,353 --> 00:36:26,053
Did someone mouth the answer to her?

1074
00:36:26,053 --> 00:36:27,253
(I can't believe it!)

1075
00:36:27,453 --> 00:36:31,093
I get the feeling you really are a rice sommelier.

1076
00:36:31,223 --> 00:36:32,563
But now I'm curious.

1077
00:36:32,563 --> 00:36:34,293
How different can these varieties of rice be?

1078
00:36:34,803 --> 00:36:37,263
- Should we go get some?
- Sounds great.

1079
00:36:39,303 --> 00:36:40,873
I'm going to go with Songhyangmi rice first.

1080
00:36:42,073 --> 00:36:44,343
Songhyangmi rice is the fancy one, right?

1081
00:36:44,343 --> 00:36:45,713
Yes, I wanted to try it.

1082
00:36:46,713 --> 00:36:48,713
I'll be a consistent person.

1083
00:36:49,083 --> 00:36:50,883
- Hangyeolmi rice!
- I pick Hangyeolmi rice.

1084
00:36:50,883 --> 00:36:52,553
(Kyung Pyo goes with Hangyeolmi.)

1085
00:36:52,983 --> 00:36:55,423
I can't pick one. There are so many choices.

1086
00:36:56,223 --> 00:36:57,883
Can I try two types of rice?

1087
00:36:57,923 --> 00:36:58,923
Yes, you can.

1088
00:36:58,923 --> 00:36:59,923
You should go for it.

1089
00:36:59,923 --> 00:37:01,893
That's why I only got a little of the first one I chose too.

1090
00:37:02,293 --> 00:37:03,323
Not bad, right?

1091
00:37:04,063 --> 00:37:07,233
I need to try this Songhyangmi rice first.

1092
00:37:07,533 --> 00:37:10,033
(Jae Seok tries the rice first.)

1093
00:37:10,133 --> 00:37:11,303
(Impressed)

1094
00:37:11,303 --> 00:37:12,803
(Nodding furiously)

1095
00:37:13,073 --> 00:37:14,943
Songhyangmi rice is a little sticky.

1096
00:37:14,943 --> 00:37:16,943
It's really glossy, unlike the others.

1097
00:37:16,943 --> 00:37:18,813
(You can see its stickiness from when you scoop the rice.)

1098
00:37:19,313 --> 00:37:21,173
Songhyangmi is delicious.

1099
00:37:21,583 --> 00:37:22,983
This is really good rice.

1100
00:37:23,583 --> 00:37:25,783
(BIBI tries a bite of Songhyangmi too.)

1101
00:37:25,813 --> 00:37:26,883
(Startled)

1102
00:37:26,883 --> 00:37:29,323
(Exclaiming)

1103
00:37:29,583 --> 00:37:30,823
- Amazing.
- It's so good.

1104
00:37:30,823 --> 00:37:32,753
This Songhyangmi rice is so good!

1105
00:37:32,753 --> 00:37:33,923
(Eyes widening)

1106
00:37:33,923 --> 00:37:34,923
Gosh!

1107
00:37:35,493 --> 00:37:37,663
I can taste butter from Songhyangmi!

1108
00:37:37,663 --> 00:37:39,593
- Right? It's so flavorful.
- I can taste butter!

1109
00:37:40,093 --> 00:37:41,603
I also get a mushroom scent.

1110
00:37:41,933 --> 00:37:42,963
I noticed too!

1111
00:37:42,963 --> 00:37:44,503
(Songhyangmi has a soft mushroom scent as well.)

1112
00:37:45,373 --> 00:37:46,703
I love that it's chewy.

1113
00:37:46,703 --> 00:37:48,103
- It's sticky and nice.
- Exactly.

1114
00:37:48,103 --> 00:37:51,073
(Songhyangmi gives more mushroom scent the more you chew.)

1115
00:37:51,713 --> 00:37:54,773
(BIBI takes a big bite of rice with kimchi.)

1116
00:37:55,443 --> 00:37:56,843
- Goodness!
- It's amazing.

1117
00:37:57,543 --> 00:37:59,613
(Opening wide)

1118
00:37:59,783 --> 00:38:01,983
It's so good. This is crazy.

1119
00:38:02,053 --> 00:38:03,453
(Another bite)

1120
00:38:03,783 --> 00:38:05,123
We might finish our meal with rice alone!

1121
00:38:05,793 --> 00:38:06,893
The side dishes are great too.

1122
00:38:07,593 --> 00:38:09,593
Good rice is delicious even with just kimchi.

1123
00:38:09,593 --> 00:38:10,963
Of course.

1124
00:38:11,263 --> 00:38:13,163
- The mackerel is here!
- Mackerel!

1125
00:38:13,163 --> 00:38:14,693
The seaweed soup looks great.

1126
00:38:14,833 --> 00:38:16,903
It says Songhyangmi goes great with mackerel.

1127
00:38:17,733 --> 00:38:20,733
We just grill our mackerel without seasoning.

1128
00:38:22,443 --> 00:38:24,643
Then it goes perfectly with the rice flavor.

1129
00:38:25,873 --> 00:38:27,843
(You can't go wrong with mackerel and seaweed soup.)

1130
00:38:27,843 --> 00:38:30,143
I love mackerel! This is perfect!

1131
00:38:30,183 --> 00:38:31,243
This place is...

1132
00:38:32,183 --> 00:38:33,253
incredible!

1133
00:38:34,013 --> 00:38:36,753
Eun I, you're great with deboning fish!

1134
00:38:36,753 --> 00:38:38,653
Yes, I'm cutting it up into chunks for you all.

1135
00:38:39,093 --> 00:38:41,153
It's better than taking a little at a time.

1136
00:38:41,153 --> 00:38:43,823
- Now you can dip it in the sauce...
- This restaurant is my type.

1137
00:38:43,893 --> 00:38:45,533
- Right.
- I really love...

1138
00:38:45,733 --> 00:38:47,693
- not doing anything when eating.
- I know.

1139
00:38:47,993 --> 00:38:49,703
Obviously, I know.

1140
00:38:49,763 --> 00:38:52,473
- I love talking and only talking.
- How can I forget?

1141
00:38:52,733 --> 00:38:54,233
My wife, Kyung Eun, always nags me.

1142
00:38:54,233 --> 00:38:55,803
I know. Kyung Eun puts up with so much.

1143
00:38:55,803 --> 00:38:58,273
- Yes, she does.
- Kyung Eun does so much.

1144
00:38:58,273 --> 00:39:00,343
I'm best friends with Kyung Eun.

1145
00:39:00,343 --> 00:39:01,473
- Really?
- Yes.

1146
00:39:01,543 --> 00:39:03,683
What did she say about her husband?

1147
00:39:03,683 --> 00:39:04,743
Well...

1148
00:39:04,743 --> 00:39:09,823
(What did Yu Jae Seok's wife say about him?)

1149
00:39:10,083 --> 00:39:13,523
She doesn't say anything bad. She really respects her husband.

1150
00:39:13,523 --> 00:39:15,093
- That's nice.
- It really is.

1151
00:39:15,093 --> 00:39:16,393
And what a great parent!

1152
00:39:16,393 --> 00:39:18,333
- I actually...
- Who? Him?

1153
00:39:18,333 --> 00:39:19,363
- No.
- No, Na Kyung Eun.

1154
00:39:19,363 --> 00:39:20,433
Right.

1155
00:39:20,593 --> 00:39:22,033
- It's Kyung Eun.
- How silly of me.

1156
00:39:22,163 --> 00:39:23,433
- Kyung Eun is a great parent.
- Yes.

1157
00:39:23,533 --> 00:39:25,203
She's so good with children,

1158
00:39:25,203 --> 00:39:26,903
I got a lot of help from her too.

1159
00:39:26,903 --> 00:39:28,273
- You don't say.
- It's true.

1160
00:39:29,103 --> 00:39:30,343
I think she made the seaweed soup herself.

1161
00:39:30,343 --> 00:39:32,843
- Is it good?
- Yes, you should try.

1162
00:39:33,043 --> 00:39:34,073
(A sip of seaweed soup)

1163
00:39:34,073 --> 00:39:35,483
You make good seaweed soup too, Ji Hye.

1164
00:39:35,513 --> 00:39:37,283
Gosh, this is so deep.

1165
00:39:37,283 --> 00:39:38,653
- Isn't it?
- Yes, it's delicious.

1166
00:39:38,653 --> 00:39:44,123
(The deep flavor of seaweed after boiling for a long time)

1167
00:39:44,953 --> 00:39:48,153
(Jeong An tries a sip of soup too.)

1168
00:39:49,263 --> 00:39:51,223
Everything here is so good!

1169
00:39:51,863 --> 00:39:52,933
Gosh.

1170
00:39:53,763 --> 00:39:55,163
The soup is great too.

1171
00:39:56,933 --> 00:39:58,063
The mackerel is divine.

1172
00:39:58,633 --> 00:39:59,903
- It's amazing.
- Isn't it?

1173
00:39:59,903 --> 00:40:00,903
Yes!

1174
00:40:00,903 --> 00:40:02,603
(A thick chunk of mackerel on warm rice)

1175
00:40:02,603 --> 00:40:03,973
This is unbelievable.

1176
00:40:04,843 --> 00:40:06,213
- Excuse me.
- The soup is so rich.

1177
00:40:06,413 --> 00:40:07,643
Thank you!

1178
00:40:08,513 --> 00:40:09,843
Stir-fried pork!

1179
00:40:10,243 --> 00:40:12,153
(Doenjang stew, a bowl of rice's best friend)

1180
00:40:12,153 --> 00:40:15,253
We put just a little doenjang in the stew...

1181
00:40:15,383 --> 00:40:16,753
and braise it down.

1182
00:40:18,653 --> 00:40:21,823
Then it goes well with the flavorful rice.

1183
00:40:22,023 --> 00:40:25,033
(Flavorful rice and doenjang)

1184
00:40:25,363 --> 00:40:26,963
(To top it off, glossy and juicy...)

1185
00:40:28,503 --> 00:40:29,803
This is going to be awesome.

1186
00:40:29,803 --> 00:40:30,833
(stir-fried pork with a spicy kick)

1187
00:40:31,133 --> 00:40:33,203
I'd love to have this restaurant in my neighborhood.

1188
00:40:33,203 --> 00:40:35,543
I'd come here every day!

1189
00:40:35,943 --> 00:40:38,443
(BIBI mixes doenjang stew with rice first.)

1190
00:40:39,173 --> 00:40:41,073
(Taking a bite)

1191
00:40:41,643 --> 00:40:42,983
(Exclaiming)

1192
00:40:43,183 --> 00:40:44,543
The stew is amazing.

1193
00:40:44,583 --> 00:40:46,653
Everything here is delicious!

1194
00:40:46,983 --> 00:40:49,183
Workers are going to love this meal.

1195
00:40:49,183 --> 00:40:50,553
The pork is so good too!

1196
00:40:51,893 --> 00:40:53,593
I think I'll come here again on my own.

1197
00:40:54,553 --> 00:40:55,593
What?

1198
00:40:56,093 --> 00:40:57,293
I think I'll come here again on my own.

1199
00:40:57,293 --> 00:40:58,963
- Right?
- I live close by too.

1200
00:40:58,963 --> 00:41:01,093
(Nodding)

1201
00:41:01,293 --> 00:41:02,533
This is a great restaurant.

1202
00:41:02,533 --> 00:41:03,903
- Exactly.
- It's amazing.

1203
00:41:03,933 --> 00:41:06,103
Workers will come here for lunch.

1204
00:41:06,103 --> 00:41:09,343
(He empties his bowl into his mouth.)

1205
00:41:09,373 --> 00:41:10,843
(Glancing)

1206
00:41:11,043 --> 00:41:12,513
(Glancing again)

1207
00:41:12,573 --> 00:41:14,943
- Hyeong Seo, can I...
- Sure, here you go.

1208
00:41:14,943 --> 00:41:17,143
- This is Jungwonjinmi rice.
- Thanks.

1209
00:41:18,143 --> 00:41:21,013
(He steals BIBI's Jungwonjinmi rice.)

1210
00:41:21,253 --> 00:41:23,783
(He finishes it in one bite,)

1211
00:41:23,823 --> 00:41:24,923
(then glances again.)

1212
00:41:26,093 --> 00:41:28,353
- Could I finish that, actually?
- Go ahead!

1213
00:41:30,123 --> 00:41:31,163
What's up?

1214
00:41:31,363 --> 00:41:33,363
He asked for some of my rice, so I gave him some.

1215
00:41:33,733 --> 00:41:36,833
But just now he asked if he could take all of it.

1216
00:41:37,503 --> 00:41:40,133
Our Kyung Pyo is letting loose again!

1217
00:41:40,473 --> 00:41:45,273
(Kyung Pyo Gone Wild: Part 2)

1218
00:41:46,073 --> 00:41:48,613
I just realized it's unlimited.

1219
00:41:49,583 --> 00:41:51,683
- That's right!
- This place is...

1220
00:41:52,013 --> 00:41:56,153
(Can 10 types of unlimited rice be real?)

1221
00:41:56,623 --> 00:41:58,823
(Pondering)

1222
00:41:59,553 --> 00:42:02,593
But the commissary fee is high here.

1223
00:42:02,893 --> 00:42:03,923
- Commissary fee?
- No, I meant...

1224
00:42:03,923 --> 00:42:04,923
(Commissary fee?)

1225
00:42:05,023 --> 00:42:07,593
(Questioning his ears)

1226
00:42:07,793 --> 00:42:09,833
- Are we in a prison?
- No, look!

1227
00:42:10,063 --> 00:42:11,233
I meant the leftover fee!

1228
00:42:12,003 --> 00:42:13,233
- What?
- You said commissary fee...

1229
00:42:13,703 --> 00:42:15,303
I don't know why that slipped out.

1230
00:42:15,503 --> 00:42:17,003
I've been looking at that sign.

1231
00:42:17,173 --> 00:42:18,513
It's five dollars per person.

1232
00:42:19,013 --> 00:42:20,773
You're saying this is real, right?

1233
00:42:20,843 --> 00:42:21,843
Exactly.

1234
00:42:21,843 --> 00:42:24,343
Say the fee was two dollars. That's too little.

1235
00:42:24,343 --> 00:42:26,913
But five dollars sounds like a real fine.

1236
00:42:26,913 --> 00:42:28,953
(A realistic leftover fee of 5 dollars)

1237
00:42:29,253 --> 00:42:30,883
- Goodness!
- It's here!

1238
00:42:30,883 --> 00:42:32,093
Thank you!

1239
00:42:32,093 --> 00:42:33,423
(Their extra order, ham and fried eggs, is here.)

1240
00:42:33,793 --> 00:42:35,363
- Ma'am?
- Yes?

1241
00:42:35,363 --> 00:42:38,693
How long has it been since you opened?

1242
00:42:38,693 --> 00:42:40,433
Since May of last year.

1243
00:42:40,433 --> 00:42:43,163
- Last year.
- It hasn't been that long.

1244
00:42:43,403 --> 00:42:44,833
Did you buy those cookers recently?

1245
00:42:44,833 --> 00:42:46,033
Oh, those...

1246
00:42:46,433 --> 00:42:50,703
(They first suspected the new cookers when they got here.)

1247
00:42:51,443 --> 00:42:56,043
(What's the story behind the newest model cookers?)

1248
00:42:56,283 --> 00:42:58,753
I used to have cookers from all different brands before.

1249
00:42:58,753 --> 00:43:00,753
- That was before.
- Did you get them for this show?

1250
00:43:00,753 --> 00:43:02,923
- No, but they got them for me.
- I see.

1251
00:43:03,423 --> 00:43:04,923
- Am I allowed to say?
- No, I get it.

1252
00:43:05,023 --> 00:43:07,323
That makes sense. Is this product placement?

1253
00:43:07,693 --> 00:43:09,093
They were brand new.

1254
00:43:09,093 --> 00:43:10,963
Yes, that's why I was suspicious.

1255
00:43:11,123 --> 00:43:13,693
When they offered, I said thank you...

1256
00:43:13,793 --> 00:43:15,903
and told them not to take them back!

1257
00:43:16,433 --> 00:43:18,633
(A cute and honest confession)

1258
00:43:18,633 --> 00:43:20,233
She's so adorable.

1259
00:43:20,433 --> 00:43:21,943
- That's so...
- Enjoy.

1260
00:43:21,943 --> 00:43:23,543
(She runs away after her shy confession.)

1261
00:43:24,273 --> 00:43:27,243
(Thank you, CUCHEN!)

1262
00:43:27,243 --> 00:43:29,043
With this restaurant...

1263
00:43:29,183 --> 00:43:30,513
- I really can't tell.
- Me neither.

1264
00:43:30,513 --> 00:43:32,183
And I hope this isn't fake.

1265
00:43:32,283 --> 00:43:34,283
When she explained everything,

1266
00:43:34,283 --> 00:43:36,823
I thought it was fake because it seemed memorized.

1267
00:43:37,023 --> 00:43:38,753
But after she got all the rice right...

1268
00:43:38,753 --> 00:43:39,923
- Exactly.
- It was incredible.

1269
00:43:40,023 --> 00:43:41,753
- She's so passionate!
- Right.

1270
00:43:41,753 --> 00:43:43,693
The way she treats her rice.

1271
00:43:43,693 --> 00:43:45,493
But the prices here...

1272
00:43:46,163 --> 00:43:48,293
I don't think you can make a profit.

1273
00:43:48,293 --> 00:43:49,803
- Right? It's too cheap.
- Yes.

1274
00:43:49,803 --> 00:43:51,203
But wait...

1275
00:43:51,703 --> 00:43:54,333
For workers who have to eat out,

1276
00:43:54,573 --> 00:43:56,273
these prices seem reasonable enough.

1277
00:43:56,273 --> 00:43:58,003
- Any higher, people won't come.
- Right.

1278
00:43:58,103 --> 00:43:59,443
